  "worked_solution": "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}v-u{v}^{\u2032}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2-3f(x)$ and $v=g(x)+1.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3{f}^{\u2032}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={g}^{\u2032}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}v-u{v}^{\u2032}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3{f}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot (g(x)+1)-(2-3f(x))\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(x)}{{(g(x)+1)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{\u2032}(4) & =\\frac{-3{f}^{\u2032}(4)\\cdot (g(4)+1)-(2-3f(4))\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(4)}{{(g(4)+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\cdot 4\\cdot (1+1)-(2-3\\cdot (-2))\\cdot 0}{{(1+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
